## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 5 |
| **Medium** | 2 |
| **Low** | 1 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is invoked — enough to hit ~95% line coverage — but almost nothing is verified. These tests will pass even if the production code is completely broken (wrong prices, lost data, corrupted CSV).

---

### Critical Findings

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (Systemic)

The entire class is designed to inflate coverage, not verify behavior. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; 3 more assert only `IsNotNull` — a trivial check that doesn't validate correctness.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE — proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER — verify it was actually stored
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

---

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)

Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price actually changed.

```csharp
// AFTER
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

---

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)

Never verifies the product is gone.

```csharp
// AFTER
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

---

#### 5. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)

A 10% discount is applied but the resulting prices are never checked. A bug like `Price * (1 + fraction)` would never be caught.

```csharp
// AFTER
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

---

#### 6. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85) & `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

`ImportFromCsv` never verifies that products are actually persisted. `GetProductCount` discards its return value.

```csharp
// ImportFromCsv — AFTER
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", imported!.Name);
